(Bug #15 regression: a function reassigning a top-level `value` global from a float to an integer must move the global's BSS tag byte. The function body's `Set` routes through the same VarDecl arm as a top-level assignment, so it shared the static-type clobber before the fix.)

a value called vg is 3.5.

To reinteger. Set vg to 1.

reinteger.

Print vg.
If vg is a number, print "num".
Otherwise print "NOT num".
If vg is a float, print "float".
Otherwise print "NOT float".